nt": "These are words you use to write about nightmares. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be at ease", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be calm and relaxed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Keeping a journal is a good way to keep my mind at ease.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le08ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "nightmare", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a bad, scary dream", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I had a nightmare last night.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le08ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "anxiety", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the feeling of worry or unease", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm suffering from sleeplessness and anxiety.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le08ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to relate to ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to connect to something else", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can relate to many causes of nightmares.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le08ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "frustrating", "type": "name"}, {"content": "annoying", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This is the most frustrating experience!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le08ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "frantically", "type": "name"}, {"content": "quickly; in a hurried way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I ran frantically through an open field.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le08ob08aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Superlatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use a superlative adjective to express the highest degree of a quality.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use a superlative adjective to talk about one thing or person in a group of things. You always use <span class=\"italic\">the</span> with the superlative.</br> Superlatives can be regular or irregular.</br> The structure of the regular superlative is:</br>   the + adjective-est</br>   or</br>     the most adjective", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Superlative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"good</br> bad</br> fine</br> scary</br> small</br> frustrating</br> intelligent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the best</br> the worst</br> the finest</br> the scariest </br>the smallest</br> the most frustrating </br>the most intelligent\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I had the scariest dream last night.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "This is the most frustrating experience!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Writing a Journal Entry", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can write a journal entry to report about interesting, stressful, or traumatic events in your life, or just to write your feelings down to put your mind at ease.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you write a journal entry, you usually <span class=\"strong\">start</span> it with the phrase \u201c<span class=\"italic\">Dear Diary</span>\u201d, like you are writing a letter to yourself.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The entry usually begins with an <span class=\"strong\">opening statement</span> (this is a summary of what you are going to write about).</br> Then you usually add some <span class=\"strong\">details</span> (use adjectives and adverbs to describe the events and your feelings).</br> When you finish your entry, you usually end with a <span class=\"strong\">closing</span> like \u201c<span class=\"italic\">Love, (your name)</span>\u201d.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a short journal entry about what kind of day you had today.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Be sure to include adjectives and adverbs to make your entry descriptive.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you want, share your entry with a partner. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a short journal entry about what I did today.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I include a lot of description to make my entry interesting.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can write about healthy habits.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can write about experiences I've had or haven't had.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can write about the quality of an object or a person and how something happens or how someone behaves.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Have you ever kept a journal? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What do you write about in your journal?   ", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], 